From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 190] panvk/kbase: debug PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_DESTROY_LAG
Generated-by: LLM

RDR1's GPU faults stop when the fragment subqueue is serialized, and the
faulting addresses are not driver buffers, which points at tiler heap
chunks freed by heap renewal while a fragment job still reads them.
PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_DESTROY_LAG=N keeps a retired heap until N more jobs
have completed on both graphics subqueues, to test that.  Debug only; a
biblioklept keeps the old catalogue a little longer.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/189

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
index 55bdc6a..171b9ef 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
@@ -2334,9 +2334,15 @@ kbase_try_destroy_retired_heap(struct panvk_gpu_queue *queue)
       kbase_subqueue_seqno_cell(queue, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_FRAGMENT)->seqno;
    uint32_t done = 0;
 
+   /* Debug: PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_DESTROY_LAG=N keeps a retired heap alive until
+    * N more jobs completed on both graphics subqueues. */
+   static int64_t lag = -1;
+   if (lag < 0)
+      lag = MAX2(debug_get_num_option("PANVK_KBASE_HEAP_DESTROY_LAG", 0), 0);
+
    while (done < queue->kbase_retired_heap_count &&
-          vt_seqno > queue->kbase_retired_heaps[done].vt_jobs &&
-          frag_seqno > queue->kbase_retired_heaps[done].frag_jobs) {
+          vt_seqno > queue->kbase_retired_heaps[done].vt_jobs + lag &&
+          frag_seqno > queue->kbase_retired_heaps[done].frag_jobs + lag) {
       kbase_kmod_csf_tiler_heap_destroy(dev->kmod.dev,
                                         queue->kbase_retired_heaps[done].ctx);
       done++;
